beta-beryllene re-relaxation at 27x27 k (2026-10-01)

The original relaxation (b-Beryllene) used an 11x11 k mesh, the other structures 25x25-33x33. A static run of that geometry
at 27x27 (b-Beryllene_k27_check, job 43605) gives forces up to 0.066 eV/A and an in-plane shear stress of 1.9 kB, and the
PBE phonon supercell (13x13 k on 5x5) a residual force of 0.045 eV/A. Same INCAR as b-Beryllene (PBE, SIGMA 0.05,
ISIF 3 with in-plane lattice freedom, EDIFFG -1E-3), only the k mesh changed. Purpose: quantify the change of lattice and
positions; the beta results downstream are kept if the change is negligible.
